@startuml request-tracing
!include _style.puml
title Trace and Correlation Propagation
autonumber
actor Client
participant Gateway
participant Scheduling
database PostgreSQL
participant "Outbox Publisher" as Publisher
queue RabbitMQ
participant "Notification Consumer" as Consumer

Client -> Gateway : request\ntraceparent optional, X-Correlation-ID optional
Gateway -> Gateway : validate/create W3C trace + correlation UUID
Gateway -> Scheduling : inject traceparent, tracestate, correlation
Scheduling -> PostgreSQL : EF span, parameterized query
PostgreSQL --> Scheduling : result
Scheduling -> PostgreSQL : Booking + Outbox\nstore correlationId/causationId/traceparent
Scheduling --> Gateway : response + correlation ID
Gateway --> Client : status + traceId in Problem Details if error

Publisher -> PostgreSQL : claim Outbox
PostgreSQL --> Publisher : event envelope
Publisher -[#6B7280,dashed]-> RabbitMQ : AMQP headers + event trace context
RabbitMQ -[#6B7280,dashed]-> Consumer : delivery
Consumer -> Consumer : create consumer span\nlink/parent producer context

note bottom
Logs chứa traceId/spanId/correlationId; metrics không label theo UUID.
Không truyền JWT, password, refresh/hold token trong baggage hoặc log.
end note
@enduml

